    "prompt": "Production asset: exactly NINE different isolated individual trees in a transparent3x3 equal-cell sprite atlas, row-major order. The supplied game building artwork is STYLE ONLY: match palette, camera, shading and painterly material treatment, but do not copy any reference subjects or ground patches.\nFixed orthographic2:1 dimetric game camera; ground axes at+26.565/-26.565 degrees, no perspective convergence. Northwest daylight, restrained warm hand-painted miniature style. Full crowns, trunks, roots and a tiny soft contact shadow are visible.\nShared physical scale with game buildings: one ground tile is16m square, an adult is1.75m and a door is2.1m. Do not draw people, doors or buildings. The normalized256px cell uses13.15px per vertical metre. Tree heights vary naturally; do not enlarge shorter species to fill their cells.\nEvery exposed trunk ROOT FOOT meets the shared horizontal baseline at95.5% of its cell height, centred horizontally. The baseline is the actual trunk foot, never the bottom of scenery. NO GRASS, SOIL, SNOW DISC, ROCKS, GROUND MOUND OR BASE PLATFORM; only the tree and a tiny contact shadow below its root. Crown and all branches stay inside their own cell with generous transparent gutters. Keep side gutters at least12% of cell width and top gutters at least10%. Tiny contact shadows fade out before the cell bottom. No long baked directional shadow; the game supplies the projected ground shadow.\nBroad asymmetrical foliage masses and clear species silhouettes readable at Region and Town zoom. A few large boughs and trunk forks; no individual leaves, fine needle lines, stippling, scratches, tiny bark fissures, tiny fruit dots, lettering or botanical labels. Each requested species has distinct branch architecture and crown proportions.\nGenuine transparent RGBA background; no coloured backdrop, checkerboard, ground rectangle, floating plinth, pots, frame, labels or UI. Exactly one whole tree per cell; no forest groups.\nCold northern woodland: cool sage and blue-green, pale bark, restrained ivory snow on upper branches and at roots. Keep tree anatomy visible.\nSlot 1: black-spruce, 13m tall, 170.9px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Narrow irregular dark blue-green spire with separated snowy branch ledges.\nSlot 2: white-spruce, 15m tall, 197.2px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Full cool sage-green conical crown with restrained ivory snow on upper boughs.\nSlot 3: mountain-hemlock, 13m tall, 170.9px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Asymmetric drooping blue-green evergreen, crooked leader and light snow.\nSlot 4: subalpine-fir, 15m tall, 197.2px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Slim dense pointed dark green crown with broad pale snow bands.\nSlot 5: siberian-larch, 14m tall, 184.1px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Open golden olive conical crown, clear horizontal branches and cool bark.\nSlot 6: tamarack, 13m tall, 170.9px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Airy narrow muted bronze-green needle crown on a tall exposed brown trunk.\nSlot 7: northern-lodgepole-pine, 14m tall, 184.1px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Thin upright rugged pine with a small narrow crown and snowy branch forks.\nSlot 8: limber-pine, 12m tall, 157.8px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Crooked open grey trunk, spreading dark needle cushions and a bent leader.\nSlot 9: bristlecone-pine, 10m tall, 131.5px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Sculptural twisted pale ancient trunk, sparse separated dark foliage cushions.",
